meta {
  name: Pretest cleanup — sweep leftover BRUNO-TEST-* fixture events (EMS)
  type: http
  seq: 0
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/admin/test-fixtures/ems/cleanup
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{authToken}}
}

headers {
  X-Correlation-ID: {{$guid}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "entityType": "events",
    "prefix": "BRUNO-TEST-"
  }
}

tests {
  test("pretest cleanup accepted (200) or gracefully missing (404)", function() {
    expect([200, 204, 404]).to.include(res.getStatus());
  });
}

docs {
  PR 13 (plan §D.11 + §B3): pretest hook sweeping leftover fixture events.
  Today's fixture event uses a server-generated BATbern{N} code (see
  01-create-fixture-event.bru), so this prefix sweep is a no-op for the current
  fixture — 99-delete-fixture-event.bru owns the per-run event teardown. The
  hook is in place for the day eventCode becomes client-suppliable (plan
  §"Risks to track" item 7).

  NOTE — there is deliberately NO pretest meetings sweep. partner_meetings has
  no Bruno-identifying column, so the cleanup endpoint targets them by an
  explicit id allowlist (entityType=meetings), which can only reach IDs created
  in the current run. Prior-run leftovers cannot be pre-swept; teardown is the
  explicit DELETE (09) + the posttest allowlist sweep (98). See README.md.
}
